# V2 data-generation contract

The active V2 generator is persistent semi-Markov play only.

- Duration: 120-180 seconds per episode; 150 seconds by default.
- Policy: exactly the same movement/camera/hold/transition implementation as V1.
- V1 capability: movement and camera bits only.
- V2 capability: the same policy with Q trajectory preview and E grenade throws.
- Grenade-control bias: Q on 30% of ordinary holds and 50% of scripted segments;
  throw opportunities are randomly spaced by 2.5-6.0 seconds after the first.
- Cooldown: the canonical two-second game cooldown is unchanged.
- Physics: one canonical launch speed and one canonical grenade simulation config.
- Outcomes: natural play only; no prescribed targets, contacts, bounces, crossings,
  rests, or arena exits.
- Validation: technical integrity, Q/E action-gate correctness, duration,
  physical throw records, and preview-versus-realized parity.
- Audit: human visual review of representative random seeds before production.

V2 has no mission catalog, cells, sequence templates, mission planner,
qualification plan, audit-slot exporter, semantic acceptance/rejection, reserve
recipes, or substitutions. Historical mission artifacts are not part of the
active contract.

See `README.md` for commands and the complete current status.
